Z||000002||rockcrawl||01-26-2001||08:23 PM||||I know what you're talking about. I'll take a look at mine tommorow. I think it is just a plastic piece on each side with a lip for the wetherstrip to attach to. I'm not sure what holds them in place though.<P>------------------<BR>Jon Lagler<BR>'87 GT<BR>4.9 liter V8 Testarossa Spyder (under construction)<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/rockcrawlsig.jpg"> ||||reg||7
Z||000003||Indiana_resto_guy||01-26-2001||08:30 PM||||OH those!<BR>They are held in place be a self threading screw that is located UNDERNEATH the side of the clip. Once the screw is removed, there is a small wedge that wraps around the edge of the sheet metal roll lip which keeps the half moon shaped pieces securely in place. If you can find some, the lower attaching bolts and the top most rearward bolts need to be removed so the rear of the clip can be lifted to gain access.||||reg||1
